/*
 * Declares the MathPointerOperatorValue class.
 *
 * MathPointerOperatorValue represents binary arithmetic operations involving at
 * least one pointer operand. These operations produce a pointer result and
 * follow pointer-arithmetic semantics rather than integer arithmetic.
 *
 * Typical supported operations include:
 *   - pointer + integer  → pointer
 *   - pointer - integer  → pointer
 *   - pointer - pointer  → integer (distance), when allowed by the language
 *
 * The operator assumes that the left operand is pointer-like, and the right
 * operand is either a pointer or an integer depending on the operator.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::pointer::math
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/pointer/math.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-03
